# The shielded offer must be the union over the call tree, not the root call's alone.
#
# 2026/09/10. Upstream: midnightntwrk/midnight-js #967 (the cross-contract call
# path) and #1025 (the callee state resolver). Reproduction and evidence:
# docs/demo/one-tx-transfer-drill.md sections 3c and 3d, and the issue text in
# docs/demo/midnight-js-callee-offer-issue.md.
#
# WHY. `createUnprovenLedgerCallTx` assembled the transaction's shielded offers
# from `nextZswapLocalState` — the ROOT call's Zswap local state — while the
# unshielded offers eleven lines above already aggregate across the whole tree
# with `calls.flatMap(...)`, for the reason the comment there gives. A callee
# that SPENDS therefore claims nullifiers that appear in no offer. Midnight
# Passport's `transfer_shielded_to_account` hits this every time the recipient
# already holds a coin of the colour being sent: the callee's `deposit_shielded`
# takes its merge branch, `mergeCoinImmediate` spends both the held coin and the
# arriving one, and the ledger's `EffectsCheck` refuses the transaction with
# `NullifiersNeqClaimedNullifiers` — node error 217. Measured on stagenet: the
# segment-0 claimed set held three nullifiers, the offer one.
#
# WHAT. The offer builder is generalised over a list of per-call states, each
# carrying its own contract address, its own Zswap local state, its own
# partitioned transcript for segment routing, and its own Zswap chain state for
# `ZswapInput.newContractOwned` — a contract-owned nullifier is derived against
# the commitment tree of the contract that OWNS the coin, so the root's will not
# do. Outputs are collected across the tree first, then inputs are paired against
# that whole set, so the root's `sendShielded` to the callee and the callee's
# spend of it become one transient rather than an unmatched pair.
# `makeCalleeStateResolver` fetches the callee's Zswap chain state alongside its
# contract state, in the one `queryZSwapAndContractState` request the provider
# pins to the same block, so the call tree is still read from one snapshot.
#
# The single-call path is unchanged by construction: `zswapStateToSegmentedOffer`
# now delegates to the new function with a one-element list, and the loop bodies
# are the originals. Checked on chain as well — rebuilding `withdraw_shielded`
# against a pinned wallet seed on the patched and unpatched builds produces the
# same nullifier, the same commitment, and the same claimed sets.
#
# Companion patch: @midnight-ntwrk+compact-js+2.5.5-rc.8.patch, which surfaces
# the per-call Zswap local state this one consumes.
